attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `relA`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 100% of them, at 0.05 bits {S1}.

@variable **A variable pair follows at `mazE` and `mazF`**, columns 1 to 2, carried by 84%, fewest named at column 1, 88% {S2}. The fork at columns 6 to 7, `ygcG` and `yqcG`, is carried by 49 to 71%, in a region of plasticity in 91 to 92% of calls {S4}. Through columns 23 to 28 a branch of 6 families runs in 18 to 29%, [[CRISPR-associated proteins]] {S10.b23, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 93 against 91%, and hesitates less there, 0.23 against 0.42 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 6, `ygcG`, a fork column, 1.86 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in fork and variable columns.** Columns 69 to 79, `ascB` to `gutM`, are carried by 64 to 85%, all persistent {S16}. The last column is `gutM`, in 64% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.32 bits on average, perplexity 1.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.68 against 0.17 bits, and names fewer genes, 85% against 95% {C}.

